# Evidence selector guard design

## DES-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-001: Deterministic first-party selector architecture scan
Responsibilities: Provide a test-support architecture scan that discovers every first-party TypeScript source under `packages/*/src/**/*.ts`, resolves uses of the path-only `evidenceInputPaths` selector to its declaration, and reports the violating repository-relative paths while allowing only the declaration and its composition inside `evidenceInputs`.
Interfaces: Internal `evidenceSelectorViolations(root: string): Promise<string[]>` in `tests/helpers/evidence-selector-architecture.ts`, consumed only by the #18-owned `tests/evidence-selector-guards.test.ts`; it enumerates with the existing deterministic `files(root)` traversal, filters paths by the first-party source pattern, constructs a TypeScript `Program` over those sources, resolves the exported `evidenceInputPaths` declaration in `packages/analysis/src/files.ts`, and uses the type checker to identify resolved value references or calls to that symbol through direct imports, aliases, namespace/property access, and computed property access.
Constraints: The scan contains no list of current consumers, package names, or expected consumer paths; a new package, source file, or renamed consumer is included solely because its path matches `packages/*/src/**/*.ts`. The only allowed resolved value-reference syntax nodes are the `evidenceInputPaths` declaration name and a reference whose nearest containing function is the `evidenceInputs` declaration in `packages/analysis/src/files.ts`; any other resolved value reference or call, including a future reference elsewhere in `files.ts`, is a violation. A module-level wildcard re-export such as `export * from './files.js'` contains no identifier reference to `evidenceInputPaths`, is not a direct consumer, and must not cause the scan to fail. Symbol identity, not identifier spelling alone, controls detection, so unrelated local names, type-only structure, comments, string literals, and identifier-free wildcard re-exports do not create violations while aliased or indirect value access cannot bypass the guard. Candidate source paths are bytewise-lexicographically sorted before program construction, and the returned repository-relative paths are deduplicated and bytewise-lexicographically sorted. A synthetic fixture contains multiple reverse-created consumer files and repeated references in one file and must produce the exact unique sorted path array. Existing `files(root)` exclusions and symbolic-link behavior remain authoritative. The scan does not change or expose a production API and does not replace the runtime selector contracts established by ADR-0018 and ADR-0021.
Requirements: REQ-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-001
ADRs: ADR-0018 ADR-0021
Depends-On: DES-M5-EVIDENCE-SKILL-001

## DES-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-002: Unified selector guard and project-status regression
Responsibilities: Add one authoritative test, `TEST-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-GUARDS-001`, that jointly proves the architecture boundary and the end-to-end stale projection for recognized repository Skill-only edits.
Interfaces: Dedicated #18-owned authoritative test file `tests/evidence-selector-guards.test.ts`; test-support scan from `DES-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-001`; existing `evidenceSnapshot(root)` and `projectStatus(root)` production entry points; existing exact repository recognition and root-aware `evidenceInputs(root)` behavior from `packages/analysis/src/files.ts`; existing quality fingerprint comparison and stale projection in `packages/analysis/src/gate.ts`.
Constraints: `tests/evidence-selector-guards.test.ts` owns the single authoritative `it` case annotated with `@id TEST-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-GUARDS-001` and `@verifies REQ-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-001 REQ-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-002`, plus all fixtures and assertions specific to these requirements. Its executable Red baseline adds the complete, subsequently unchanged dedicated test together with a callable `evidenceSelectorViolations` stub that returns `[]`: a synthetic repository containing reverse-created `packages/example/src/direct-consumer.ts` and `packages/renamed/src/alias-consumer.ts` files, including repeated direct, aliased, and namespace references, must instead yield the exact unique sorted violating paths, so Vitest fails on that behavioral assertion rather than on compilation or import setup. Green replaces only the test-support stub with the TypeScript symbol scan, preserves the negative fixture assertion, and additionally scans the real repository, where the result must be `[]`; therefore the same passing test proves both that violations are detectable and that no current first-party consumer bypasses `evidenceInputs`, without a hard-coded consumer list. `tests/evidence-skill-inputs.test.ts` remains #25-owned for `REQ-M5-EVIDENCE-009` migration and exclusion coverage; this change neither moves the new authoritative test into that file nor edits, renames, re-annotates, or expands its existing test ownership.

For the end-to-end branch, the same test creates a minimal temporary repository with the exact ADR-0018 `musubix5` manifest identity, compatible approval configuration, one ordinary source file, `.github/skills/example/SKILL.md`, and any minimal artifacts needed by `projectStatus`. After all non-evidence fixture inputs exist, it obtains the authoritative fingerprints through `evidenceSnapshot(root)` and writes schema-version-1 quality evidence with `status: pass`, a non-empty set of passing required checks, and those fingerprints. The first direct `projectStatus(root)` call must return `gate.status: pass` and `gate.ready: true`. Changing only `.github/skills/example/SKILL.md` and calling `projectStatus(root)` again must return `gate.status: stale` and `gate.ready: false`; the assertion must not call `qualityInputsCurrent` directly or substitute a unit-level projection for `projectStatus`.

The same authoritative test preserves exclusion behavior with isolated current-fingerprint fixtures: changing a non-`SKILL.md` file below `.github/skills/` in a recognized repository leaves `projectStatus(root).gate` at `{ status: 'pass', ready: true }`, and changing `SKILL.md` under an unrecognized repository identity also leaves the gate at `{ status: 'pass', ready: true }`. Quality evidence is written only after each fixture's complete initial input set is present, `.musubix/evidence/quality.json` remains excluded as gate self-evidence, timestamps are fixed, no Git state or network access participates, and temporary directories are removed through the existing cleanup pattern. Existing `TEST-M5-EVIDENCE-SKILL-FINGERPRINT-001` coverage remains intact; only the new test is authoritative for these two requirements.
Implementation-Handoff: Create `tests/evidence-selector-guards.test.ts` and `tests/helpers/evidence-selector-architecture.ts` for the #18 Red/Green batch. Keep `tests/evidence-skill-inputs.test.ts` unchanged and outside the batch because its `TEST-M5-EVIDENCE-SKILL-FINGERPRINT-001` node and migration-exclusion assertions remain owned by #25 and `REQ-M5-EVIDENCE-009`.
Requirements: REQ-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-001 REQ-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-002
ADRs: ADR-0018 ADR-0021
Depends-On: DES-M5-WAVE1-EVIDENCE-001 DES-M5-EVIDENCE-SKILL-001
